1065
01:32:36,336 --> 01:32:42,404
And currently in the CRM system, I have the ability to see my contacts, but I can't see my coworkers' contacts for whatever reason.

1066
01:32:42,576 --> 01:32:45,456
There's limits on what I can see in the system, right?

1067
01:32:45,536 --> 01:32:47,616
Where my manager maybe could see more information.

1068
01:32:47,854 --> 01:32:55,620
We need to make sure we don't build an agent that now gives me the ability to see my manager's information or my colleagues' contacts.

1069
01:32:55,918 --> 01:33:00,816
The agent should practice least privilege, that it shouldn't overprivilege anything.

1070
01:33:00,976 --> 01:33:05,936
Kind of built on top of that is this concept of RBAC or role-based access control.

1071
01:33:06,096 --> 01:33:10,416
And really, this is the security model that enforces the concept of least privilege.

1072
01:33:10,576 --> 01:33:25,444
And this is saying that, hey, based on somebody's job title or their work, like their job, what they do, their requirements, that this that person only has access to the resources that are actually required for them to perform their responsibilities.

1073
01:33:25,710 --> 01:33:38,016
So this is the actual like practical enforcement of least privilege and that the control, we are controlling the access somebody has based on their role, role-based access control.

