Well, maybe that agent costs you $200,000 to build, right?

1788
02:32:02,896 --> 02:32:07,776
And it only really saves you a couple thousand dollars a month in copilot credit costs compared to what it makes you, right?

1789
02:32:07,856 --> 02:32:10,496
Like you're at a net loss of total cost of ownership.

1790
02:32:10,656 --> 02:32:22,096
A lot of times, too, you will see at the beginning, return on investment might be a lot lower because there might be a lot of, you know, investment into the data estate, into the team's upskilling and those sort of things.

1791
02:32:22,176 --> 02:32:31,616
And maybe your agents at the beginning have to eat a lot of those costs, where agents later on don't have to, you know, there wasn't any data preparation in the development of that agent because it was done for a development of.

1792
02:32:32,112 --> 02:32:33,412
Of a previous agent, so to speak.

1793
02:32:33,582 --> 02:32:36,752
So just things to think about in terms of total cost of ownership.

1794
02:32:36,912 --> 02:32:48,752
And so bringing it back then to an agent development framework as we think about this, we need to not only think about, you know, yes, defining business outcomes, but when we talk about that, we need to define the ROA drivers, right?

1795
